    "result_text": "All done. The build is green (only `AcceptanceTest` exists, and it passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string membership *tier* with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed as: start at 1, +1 if an email is present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility domain helper (`MembershipLevel.of(Owner)`), mirroring the existing `Locality` helper. Encapsulates the level formula in one place so both the response mapping and the audit line reuse it rather than duplicating the rule.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` mapping/method (with its GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE `householdSize` logic) is replaced by `membershipLevel(Owner)` returning `Integer` (null-safe for MapStruct), delegating to `MembershipLevel.of`.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (via the shared helper) instead of carrying tier information.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the `Owner` schema's `membershipTier` string enum is replaced by an integer `membershipLevel` property (which regenerates `OwnerDto` without `MembershipTierEnum`), so the response now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer `membershipTier`.\n\nThe new `coreNumericLevel` test (owner with email + no namesakes \u2192 level 3) passes, and the audit output confirms `membershipLevel=3`.\n\nNote: the old tier had a GOLD rule driven by `householdSize >= 3`; the new specification's formula makes no mention of household size, so that input no longer affects the level \u2014 matching the spec's \"start at 1; +email; +namesakeCount==0; cap 3\" exactly.",
